From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 02:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] drm/msm/dpu: Add a debugfs trigger for the display
 snapshot

msm_disp_snapshot_state() captures the whole DPU register state into a
devcoredump, but the only things that call it are the iommu fault handler
and the encoder frame-done and ctl-start timeouts. A fault that corrupts
the scanned-out image without ever raising an interrupt is therefore
invisible to it, which is exactly the case where the register state is
worth having.

Add a write-only debugfs file that calls it, so a snapshot can be taken
while the display is still in the bad state:

  echo 1 > /sys/kernel/debug/dri/<dev>/debug/disp_snapshot
  cat /sys/class/devcoredump/devcd*/data > dump.txt

Written for a half-screen colour corruption on an X1E80100 laptop that
leaves the composited buffer intact and the DP link parameters unchanged,
and so has to be diffed out of the mixer-to-interface datapath.

Signed-off-by: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
@@ -288,6 +288,23 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * The register snapshot is otherwise only reachable from an iommu fault or an
+ * encoder timeout, which is no help for a fault that corrupts the image without
+ * ever raising one. Writing here captures the same devcoredump on demand, so a
+ * glitch can be caught while it is still on screen.
+ */
+static int dpu_kms_snapshot_set(void *data, u64 val)
+{
+	struct drm_device *dev = data;
+
+	if (val)
+		msm_disp_snapshot_state(dev);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+DEFINE_DEBUGFS_ATTRIBUTE(dpu_kms_snapshot_fops, NULL, dpu_kms_snapshot_set, "%llu\n");
+
 static int dpu_kms_debugfs_init(struct msm_kms *kms, struct drm_minor *minor)
 {
 	struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms = to_dpu_kms(kms);
@@ -305,6 +322,9 @@
 
 	debugfs_create_x32(DPU_DEBUGFS_HWMASKNAME, 0600, entry, p);
 
+	debugfs_create_file("disp_snapshot", 0200, entry, minor->dev,
+			    &dpu_kms_snapshot_fops);
+
 	dpu_debugfs_danger_init(dpu_kms, entry);
 	dpu_debugfs_vbif_init(dpu_kms, entry);
 	dpu_debugfs_core_irq_init(dpu_kms, entry);
-- 
